filogic: give the BPI-R4 Pro 4E Wi-Fi a per-board MAC

11_fix_wifi_mac derives the MT7996 (BE14) PHY address from eth0 for the
BPI-R4 family but not for the R4 Pro, so the card kept the placeholder
address of the default EEPROM image (00:0c:43:26:60:x0). Every R4 Pro then
advertised the same BSSIDs; a 4E next to an 8X shared 00:0c:43:26:60:10 and
:20 on the same channels and clients could associate but never finish the
WPA handshake. Reuse the BPI-R4 rule (eth0 + 2/3/4 per PHY).

--- a/target/linux/mediatek/filogic/base-files/etc/hotplug.d/ieee80211/11_fix_wifi_mac
+++ b/target/linux/mediatek/filogic/base-files/etc/hotplug.d/ieee80211/11_fix_wifi_mac
@@ -69,7 +69,8 @@
 		;;
 	bananapi,bpi-r4|\
 	bananapi,bpi-r4-2g5|\
-	bananapi,bpi-r4-poe)
+	bananapi,bpi-r4-poe|\
+	bananapi,bpi-r4-pro-4e)
 		addr=$(cat /sys/class/net/eth0/address)
 		[ "$PHYNBR" = "0" ] && macaddr_add $addr 2 > /sys${DEVPATH}/macaddress
 		[ "$PHYNBR" = "1" ] && macaddr_add $addr 3 > /sys${DEVPATH}/macaddress
